// BrazeFX — Phase 2b fire/smoke solver (voxel-space velocity).
// Fields texture: .x density, .y temperature, .z fuel, .w burn (emission signal).
// Velocity texture: .xyz velocity in VOXELS / second.
//
// Per frame (driven by BrazeSolver.cs):
//   Mark occupancy -> Advect -> Emit(source-local motion) -> Force(+clamp)
//        -> Divergence -> RBGS xN (red+black) -> Project -> Curl -> Decay
//
// Multiple emitters and forces are packed into StructuredBuffers and looped per voxel,
// mirroring the publisher-owned three-js-volume prototype's per-voxel emitter/force evaluation.
// Combustion + decay constants are adapted from its GpuSolver.ts (unit-free per-second rates).

